OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F428A1787748977
OL,1,W5j 5Qwsj#%7k"k#j  w{j#57i
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q,.*,%-. * *,$%** %-& (,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSAFires still burn in charred
OL,4,Alandscape as focus turns to wildfire
OL,5,Aprevention
OL,6,
OL,7,FIt's one of several hot-spots which
OL,8,Fkeeps emerging a full week after
OL,9,Ffirefighters left the scene, which Ben
OL,10,Flikens to a game of whack-a-mole in an
OL,11,Falready charred landscape where the
OL,12,Fsmell of burning still hangs heavily in
OL,13,Fthe air.
OL,15,FBut while the small pockets of
OL,16,Fsmouldering vegetation are still being
OL,17,Fdealt with, attention is turning to
OL,18,Fimproving wildfire protection.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,429,420,260,160,0,100
